<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-mistakes-are-tools-for-learning> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-mistakes-are-tools-for-learning> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 7." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-mistakes-are-tools-for-learning> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff models this — he will say 'I was wrong about X' and redirect without defending the prior position. Invites pushback rather than fending it off." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-mistakes-are-tools-for-learning> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Gates, hooks, ceremony ROI audits, three-role interaction as mutual correction. The seams between roles generate the corrections. Self-regulation: systems correct themselves from their own signal; unwanted feedback is still information." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-mistakes-are-tools-for-learning> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Mistakes are tools for learning" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-mistakes-are-tools-for-learning> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Evaluate your trials. Making mistakes is a sign you're trying to do things better. There is usually little penalty for mistakes if you learn from them." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-mistakes-are-tools-for-learning> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
