<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff reads the board, looks at the screenshare, listens to stories before committing to a move. Decision-making starts with watching. Resists 'give me the first step' when the shape isn't clear yet." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Gemba, dashboards, mutual attention. Watch a role work before directing it. Read the board before acting on it. Loom principles → architecture → code: pattern cards before implementation cards; composition before primitives." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Observe" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Use protracted and thoughtful observation rather than prolonged and thoughtless action. In the garden, this may mean noting where the sun and its shade fall during the day, where water collects, and in which direction the winds blow. Think over seasons, years." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-observe> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
