<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "Jeff looks for root-cause invariants rather than surface fixes. The preference for 'fix the shape that causes the bug, not the bug.' Calls out agent-shaped solutions that mass-mutate instead of adjusting the rule." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Fix the invariant once, not the symptom repeatedly. One-line inventory exclude beats 2075-file front-matter prepend. Gates over sweeps." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Make the least change for the greatest effect" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Understand the system you are working with well enough to find its 'leverage points' and intervene there, where the least work accomplishes the most change." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-least-change-greatest-effect> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
