<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#order> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#source> "Hemenway, T. Gaia's Garden, 2nd ed., p. 6." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#jeffReading> "When Jeff has a live insight (a thought, write, reading), he cards it or stories it. The 2-month rule: capture-while-warm, not-on-discipline. Retires things — principles, cards, protocols, names — when they stop producing." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#techReading> "Capture events, insights, and decisions while warm — Chorus index, spine events, memory records, stories. TTL. Produce-no-waste corollary: every output of one element is input to another. Retire what does not earn its place." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#label> "Catch and store energy and materials" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#comment> "Identify, collect, and hold useful flows. Every cycle is an opportunity for yield; every gradient (in slope, charge, temperature, or otherwise) is an opportunity for energy." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#ownedBy> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#principal-wren> <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-08T16:13:36Z" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Identify, collect, and hold useful flows. Every cycle is an opportunity for yield; every gradient (in slope, charge, temperature, or otherwise) is an opportunity for energy." <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
<https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#hemenway-catch-and-store> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Catch and store energy and materials" <urn:chorus:domains:principles> .
